 CEDAR RIDGE REGIONAL TRANSMISSION SYSTEM
 SCADA / CONTROL SYSTEM DESCRIPTION
 Doc. ENG-SCADA-001  |  Rev. 5  |  2025-10-02
 Author: M. Oyelaran, SCADA/Controls Engineer   Reviewed: W. Pruitt, PE
==============================================================================

1. PROCESS OVERVIEW
-------------------

  Cedar River --> Intake PS-1 --24" raw main--> Cedar Ridge WTP --16" transmission main-->
                  (PLC01)                       (PLC02 chem feed)
      --> Hilltop Booster PS-3 --> Summit Elevated Tank --> 4 member towns
          (RTU03)                   (1.0 MG, 40 ft)

1.1 Cedar River Intake Pump Station (PS-1)
    Location: River Rd at the Cedar River bridge
    Three 3-MGD vertical turbine pumps (P-101, P-102, P-103) draw from a
    screened wet well. Lead/lag control on wet-well level with a low-low
    level trip to protect the pumps from running dry (cavitation destroys a
    vertical turbine pump in seconds). Normally P-101 lead, P-102 lag,
    P-103 standby. Raw water is delivered through a 24" main to the WTP.

1.2 Cedar Ridge Water Treatment Plant (WTP)
    Location: 1200 Plant Rd, Cedar Ridge.  Rated capacity 9.0 MGD.
    Conventional treatment: coagulation (alum), flocculation, sedimentation,
    dual-media filters (4), clearwell. Chemical feed controller PLC02 doses:
      - Sodium hydroxide (25% NaOH) for pH / corrosion control. Normal dose
        approx. 100 ppm, finished-water pH ~8.0. HMI operator limit 0-200 ppm.
        A high-high pH cutout stops the caustic pump at pH 9.5.
      - Chlorine (gas, vacuum feed) for disinfection, ~1.5 mg/L.
    Finished water is pumped from the clearwell into the 16" transmission main.

1.3 16-inch Transmission Main
    4.0 km (13,200 ft) of 16" ductile iron, EXCEPT the Miller Creek crossing,
    which is a 1962 cast-iron segment awaiting replacement (FY29 capital
    plan). The main is susceptible to water hammer; see
    Projects\Hilltop_Surge_Study_2019_SUMMARY.txt.

1.4 Hilltop Booster Pump Station (PS-3) and Summit Elevated Tank
    Location: 8042 Hilltop Rd.
    Two booster pumps (P-301, P-302), flow control valve FCV-301 and surge
    anticipator valve SAV-301 discharging to the 1.0 MG Summit Elevated Tank
    (40 ft bowl, overflow at 38 ft). Pumps run lead/lag on tank level.
    Protective functions in RTU03 logic:
      - Pump high discharge pressure trip (140 psi)
      - Tank high-level pump cutoff (35 ft)
      - SAV-301 armed (opens on pressure transients)
      - FCV-301 slew-rate limit (2 %/s)
    Protective settings are enforced by the RTU logic and can only be changed
    with the station maintenance mode enabled from the engineering
    workstation (maintenance key - see ENG-SCADA-004, kept on ww-eng01).

