3. SUPERVISORY SYSTEMS
----------------------
 ww-hmi01  ({{ ww_net }}.40.10)  AquaView HMI. Polls all controllers over Modbus/TCP
                         every 1 s. Operator screens, alarming, shift log.
                         Exposes a read-only tag API to the historian.
 ww-hist01 ({{ ww_net }}.30.10)  AquaHistorian. Collects tags from the HMI tag API and
                         serves trend pages to the corporate network (:8080).
 ww-eng01  ({{ ww_net }}.40.20)  Engineering workstation. PLC/RTU project files,
                         programming tools, project backups.

4. CONTROL PHILOSOPHY
---------------------
 - Pumps have three modes: OFF / HAND / AUTO. In AUTO the controller runs
   the pump on level. HAND starts are commanded from the HMI and bypass the
   level-based start/stop (protective trips still apply).
 - Setpoints entered at the HMI are range-checked by the HMI only. The
   controllers accept any value written over Modbus/PCOM.
 - Loss of communications: controllers continue in AUTO on last setpoints.

